\newlabel{fig:system}{{1}{2}{\textbf {\sys {} architecture.} (1)~$\sigma _u$ holds one read-only trunk; \texttt {fork} aliases it in $O(1)$; LCP binds the winner. (2)~A residual exits at the first decisive action. $m_i=\ell _i$ is $\mathrm {HS}$ ($\Work {=}0$); $0{<}m_i{<}\ell _i$ is $\mathrm {HP}$; a clean low score is $\mathrm {DS}$; the first $\alpha \ell _i$ failing is $\mathrm {EA}$; otherwise $\mathrm {PF}$ prefills $\ell _i$ on the alias. Index $0$ stays in $\Keep $, and $\Xfer $ sums $\Work _i$ only over that kept set. (3)~Slots are $C=\lfloor H/M_{\mathrm {spine}}\rfloor $; $B^c_t$ runs beside $B^s_t$, and a known suffix is pinned when $p{=}1$ and $\Pref \le \Idle $. After abort the live occupancy is the spine; the same pool admits $76{\to }103$ sessions}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:system@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][1][]2}{}{}{}}
